A||||6||kempo||Car Alarm shopping questions..||||1||
Z||000000||kempo||09-18-2001||08:41 AM||||I am looking into getting an alarm for my fiero.  What I want is something that will be able to switch from proximity to a regular (impact) alarm, with keyless entry.  Variable settings would be great, and I want this thing to be LOUD.  I've looked at some K-9 systems, a few Viper systems, but nothing is really floating my boat.  Are there any brands out there that will do what I want it to?  I was thinking about this system,<BR> <A HREF="http://cgi.ebay.com/aw-cgi/eBayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&item=1274613601" TARGET=_blank>http://cgi.ebay.com/aw-cgi/eBayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&item=1274613601</A> <P>and I don't care for remote start.  What brands should I check out and consider?  I'm looking to spend about $200, a little more if needed.  Are there any other features that I would want in a car alarm?  Thanks!<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.admist.net/kempsig.jpg"> <BR>87 Fiero GT / 5 Speed<BR>86 Fiero 2m4 - FOR SALE||||reg||1
Z||000001||85ZainoGT||09-18-2001||09:52 PM||||ewow, that looks awesome!||||reg||1
Z||000002||Haagster||09-19-2001||06:03 AM||||Looks good, but who manufacturers it?  I've been looking at Code Alarm for my 87GT.  Has most of the same features (for a price), plus it is a name brand (I learned that lesson from buying computer parts 10 years ago from "Reveal" - old sub-standard junk that didn't perform as expected or advertised).  Before you drop that kind of change, know what you are getting!!!<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Signature_4.jpg"> ||||reg||6
Z||000003||rogergarrison||09-19-2001||06:45 AM||||Personally, I dont like alarms. They arent reliable, go off when unnecessary and dont when there supposed to. Ive had some  very expensive ones that were more of a nuisance than anything else. 90% of people pay no attention to one going off anyway, and Ive even seen kids in a parking lot setting off the talking ones just to listen to them. Pager may be better, but thats if the signal gets to you inside a building. It wont stop a thief either, almost are very ez to disable. The only part of one worthwhile would be one that unlocks doors too by remote, but even those arent reliable. Id save the money, watch where you park, buy something more useful. Lisa got one this summer and Im pretty sure she said its not working already.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Phil||09-19-2001||06:50 AM||||easier to put a hidden switch in the fuel pump circuit.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Oreif||09-19-2001||09:17 AM||||Alarms only keep "honest people honest". If a professional car thief wants your car it's gone. As for kids and vandals, It can deter most of them. The big key to having a good alarm system is to install it yourself. Most alarm install shops install the items in the same location on all cars of the same model. So all they need to do is buy an alarm and have the shop install it. then take it home and see how to by-pass it. Hide the control box in a spot not easily accessed. (Most thieves won't spend more than 1 minute of time on a car) Solder all the wires and wrap them into the cars harness. The "qwik-clips" most alarm places use will cause problems inside 6 months. Keep the shock sensor sensitivity set low (to keep it from going off every time the wind blows).<BR>I have had my Chapman Alarm in my car for 5 years, no problems. I installed one in my Mom's car back in 1990 and it still works fine today. Go for quality not gadgets. <BR><P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">    <BR><B><I>Got Emblems?</I></B>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Leadfoot||09-19-2001||10:35 AM||||Speaking of alarms...I was wondering if alarm systems like the Viper are available "uninstalled" to the public?  I have one in my jeep that crapped out.  So far my jeep has been broken into twice.  The second time they tried to drive away with it.  Looks like the guy tried to undo the back window but decided to go in through the back side window.  He probable got half way in when the interior motion sensor was tripped.  Anyways I remeber J.C. Whiteny use to sell a paging alarm system.  I would rather have something like that because even if you can hear your alarm go off you at least can hear the beeper.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
